 their allies on November the 5th  British and French paratroopers were  dropped into the area around the canal  to secure it so the Egyptian army wasn't  really prepared to resist the well-armed  and well-trained militaries of the three  nations attacking him and they were  quickly overrun however the population  of Egypt rallied around nasara many  civilians took to resisting the invaders  even passively or even taking up arms  themselves the military side of the  conflict was over quickly with Israel  France and the UK achieving their  objectives  politically though it was a nightmare  for them most nations across the world  sided with Egypt and the USSR even  threatened to use nuclear weapons  against Britain and France  Dwight D Eisenhower the US president was  absolutely livid with the British and  French and even went so far as to  threaten to kick them both out of NATO  furthermore Eisenhower threatened to  sell-off sterling bonds which would have  severely harmed the value of  pound which in turn would have likely  crashed the British economy as a result  Britain immediately ceased hostilities  in France and Israel une after signed a  ceasefire British and French forces left  Egypt in late November and his road  didn't withdraw from the Sinai  peninsular until March of the next year  the Suez Crisis was over for Britain the  Suez Crisis was a disaster and  demonstrated that it could no longer  pursue its own foreign policy without  the consent of the United States the  crisis would also end the career of  Anthony Eden for France the effects were  similar and Malay wouldn't last much  longer than Eden for Israel the war was  much more profitable his Rao's  capabilities were now demonstrated to  its neighbors and whilst Israel still  couldn't use the Suez Canal it could now  use the straight tooth to run which  Egypt had previously broke Aidid since  1950 the crisis also saw the expansion  of the UN's duties and importance in  international diplomacy the crisis of  the UN send an international force of  peacekeepers the first of its kind to  the region to calm and monitor the  situation as for Egypt a more  specifically NASA the crisis was an  unparalleled victory NASA was now seen  as the Arab world's defender against  colonial aggressors and his popularity  soared this in turn would see him become  the face of the pan-arab East movement  which would briefly see the unification  of Egypt of Syria but that's a story for  a different time I hope you enjoyed this  episode and thank you for watching a  special thanks to James Bissonnette  ozark a flash Henry Robin Winston Cawood  Adam Harvey and Skye Chappell  you
 

